  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="aa770c91-6152-463d-9f99-edbe3fb79379" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Solve each equation and write the solutions using the ± notation, then choose the correct solution from the list.</para>
            <para>\(x^2=144\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 144\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 72\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 12\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 24\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \pm\; 12\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(x= \pm\; 12\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9c17d561-1f7d-4b84-a828-eb6bc2674a19" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x^2=5\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt{5}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 5\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{5}{2}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt{10}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{5}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{5}\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5a29821c-570d-4176-b0ad-403f43515e37" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(4x^2=28\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt {\frac{7}{2}}\)</para>
            <para>\( x= \pm\; 7\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{7}{2}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt{7}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{7}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{7}\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c8664b91-9471-408e-8c77-c482d15e691b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(x^2=\frac{25}{4}\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{25}{4}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{5}{2}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{10}{2}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{5}{4}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \pm\; \frac{5}{2}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(x= \pm\; \frac{5}{2}\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_09ef6dde-3940-48ed-97eb-ffffc682c2d7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(2x^2=22\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt{\frac{11}{2}}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 11\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac{11}{2}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt{11}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{11}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{11}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5a8ed6eb-d457-4dca-a7ae-6ff48710eb3a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(7x^2=16\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \sqrt{\frac{16}{7}}\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 16\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; 8\)</para>
            <para>\(x= \pm\; \frac {\sqrt{16}}{7}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{\frac{16}{7}}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(x= \pm\; \sqrt{\frac{16}{7}}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_20fac294-8500-40b9-9be9-801062d93322" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For each expression, choose an equivalent expression.</para>
            <para>\(10 \pm \sqrt{4}\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>-17 and 5</para>
            <para>\(4+ \sqrt{2}\) and \(4- \sqrt{2}\)</para>
            <para>8 and 12</para>
            <para>3 and 5</para>
            <para>\(4+ \sqrt{10}\) and \(4- \sqrt{10}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 8 and 12</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: 8 and 12.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1d3cc2ba-12ad-404c-ba1d-48d5c65f7deb" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(4 \pm \sqrt{10}\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>-17 and 5</para>
            <para>\(4+ \sqrt{2}\) and \(4- \sqrt{2}\)</para>
            <para>8 and 12</para>
            <para>3 and 5</para>
            <para>\(4+ \sqrt{10}\) and \(4- \sqrt{10}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(4+ \sqrt{10}\) and \(4- \sqrt{10}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(4+ \sqrt{10}\) and \(4- \sqrt{10}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_46a3bfd3-b470-45a0-af0e-3026a58aed89" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(\sqrt{16} \pm \sqrt{2}\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>-17 and 5</para>
            <para>\(4+ \sqrt{2}\) and \(4- \sqrt{2}\)</para>
            <para>8 and 12</para>
            <para>3 and 5</para>
            <para>\(4+ \sqrt{10}\) and \(4- \sqrt{10}\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(4+ \sqrt{2}\) and \(4- \sqrt{2}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(4+ \sqrt{2}\) and \(4- \sqrt{2}\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d5a44196-2396-47d2-90b8-0c135a49cdd2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the difference between \(\sqrt{9}\) and the solutions to \(x^2=9\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\sqrt{9}\) is equal to 3, while \(x^2=9\) is equal to -3.</para>
            <para>\(\sqrt{9}\) is equal to -3, while there are two numbers that make \(x^2=9\) true: 3 and -3.</para>
            <para>\(\sqrt{9}\) is equal to 3, while there are two numbers that make \(x^2=9\) true: 3 and -3.</para>
            <para>There is no difference; they are equal.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(\sqrt{9}\) is equal to 3, while there are two numbers that make \(x^2=9\) true: 3 and -3.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: \(\sqrt{9}\) is equal to 3, while there are two numbers that make \(x^2=9\) true: 3 and -3..</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5828e49f-09bc-4b72-b74e-42464e580ef1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Technology required. For each equation, find the exact solutions by completing the square and the approximate solutions by graphing. Then, verify that the solutions found using the two methods are close.</para>
            <para>Solve the equation \(x^2+10x+8=0\) by completing the square.<emphasis>Select two</emphasis> exact solutions.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x= -5+ \sqrt{17}\), \(x= -5- \sqrt{17}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x= -5+ \sqrt{17}\), \(x= -5- \sqrt{17}\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8b10c10d-c9c2-4abe-8642-97d37b21e99f" class="multiple-choice">
