        <exercise id="_9b88a133-7601-4a81-aaf9-41c2a596d0a0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Are the solutions and the graph for the equation \(x^2+10x+8=0\) similar?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>They are not similar.</para>
            <para>They are similar because the solutions are close.</para>
            <para>They are not similar because the square root of a number is always positive.</para>
            <para>They are similar because the square root of a number is always positive.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! They are similar because the solutions are close. \(-5- \sqrt{17} \approx -9.123\) and \(-5+ \sqrt{17} \approx -0.877\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.5.3 and 9.5.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: They are similar because the solutions are close. \(-5- \sqrt{17} \approx -9.123\) and \(-5+ \sqrt{17} \approx -0.877\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1dd47cdf-1502-4859-b8b9-851a99c3e986" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Answer the following questions about \(x^2-4x-11=0\).</para>
            <para>Solve the equation \(x^2-4x-11=0\) by completing the square.<emphasis>Select two</emphasis> exact solutions.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(x=2+ \sqrt{15}\), \(x=2-\sqrt{15}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.5.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(x=2+ \sqrt{15}\), \(x=2-\sqrt{15}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
