        <exercise id="e34dd45b-d934-43e2-a0c2-00692e36905a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Are the solutions and the graph for the equation \(x^2-4x-11=0\) similar?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>They are similar because the solutions are close</para>
            <para>They are not similar because the square root of a number is always positive.</para>
            <para>They are not similar.</para>
            <para>They are similar because the square root of a number is always positive.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! They are similar because the solutions are close. \(2-\sqrt{15} \approx -1.873\) and \(2+ \sqrt{15} \approx 5.873\).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.5.3 and 9.5.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is:They are similar because the solutions are close. \(2-\sqrt{15} \approx -1.873\) and \(2+ \sqrt{15} \approx 5.873\). You seem to be struck. Who can you ask for help?</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
